    "chunk_size_bytes": 1976,
    "chunk_text": "(a) the procedure to be followed in relation to a request received by a controller from a data subject under section 13, 14, 15, 16 or 18 of the principal enactment; and\n\n(b) such request to be complied with by the controller free of charge, except in certain circumstances.\n\nClause 6 : This clause amends section 19 of the principal enactment and the legal effect of this section as amended is to provide further for a data subject to appeal to the Authority in respect of a refusal to provide access to personal data under section 13 and to allow withdrawal of consent under section 14(1).\n\nClause 7 : This clause amends section 20 of the principal enactment and the legal effect of this section as amended is-\n\n(a) to dispense with the requirement to designate or appoint a Data Protection Officer where the processing is carried out by a public corporation; and\n\n(b) to provide for the requirement to appoint or designate a Data Protection Officer where the core activities of processing carried out by the controller or processor consists of categories of processing which results in a risk of harm affecting the rights of the data subjects.\n\nClause 8 : This clause amends section 24 of the principal enactment and the legal effect of this section as amended is to provide for a personal data protection impact assessment to be submitted to the Authority only upon a written request of the Authority.\n\nClause 9 : This clause amends section 25 of the principal enactment and the legal effect of this section as amended is-\n\n(a) to limit the application of that section in respect of risk of harm to the rights of data subjects guaranteed under the principal enactment; and\n\n(b) to repeal subsections (2), (3), (4), (5) and (6) thereof.\n\nClause 10 : This clause replaces section 26 of the principal enactment and the legal effect of this section as replaced is to specify the requirements to be complied with by a controller or processor engaged in cross-border data flows."
