    "chunk_text": "1National Minimum Wage of Workers (Amendment)\n\nNATIONAL MINIMUM WAGE OF WORKERS\n\n(AMENDMENT)\n\nA\n\nBILL\n\nto amend the National Minimum Wage of Workers Act, No. 3 of 2016\n\n\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\n\nPresented by the Minister of Labour on 03rd of June, 2025\n\n(Published in the Gazette on May 20, 2025)\n\nOrdered by Parliament to be printed\n\n\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\n\nPARLIAMENT OF THE DEMOCRATIC\n\nSOCIALIST REPUBLIC OF\n\nSRI LANKA\n\n\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\n\nprinted at the department of government printing, sri lanka\n\nto be purchased at the government publications bureau, colombo 5Price : Rs. 12.00 Postage : Rs. 150.00\n\nThis Bill can be downloaded from www.documents.gov.lk\n\n[Bill No. 13]\n\nNational Minimum Wage of Workers (Amendment)2\n\nSTATEMENT OF LEGAL EFFECT\n\nClause 2: This clause amends section 3 of the National Minimum Wage of Workers Act, No. 3 of 2016 and the legal effect of that section as amended to increase the national minimum monthly wage by Rs. 9,500 and national minimum daily wage by Rs. 380 with effect from April 1, 2025 to December 31, 2025 and further to increase the national minimum monthly wage by Rs. 3000 and national minimum daily wage by Rs. 120 with effect from January 1, 2026.\n\nClause 3: This clause is to consolidate the budgetary relief allowances as part of the wage of the workers.\n\n1National Minimum Wage of Workers (Amendment)\n\n2 - PL 15286 - 455 (06/2025)\n\nShort title and date of operation\n\nAmendment of section 3 of Act, No. 3 of 2016\n\nInclusion of the budgetary relief allowances in the national minimum monthly wage\n\nL.D.- O 18/2025\n\nAn Act to amend the National Minimum Wage of\n\nWorkers Act, No. 3 of 2016\n\nBE it enacted by the Parliament of the Democratic Socialist Republic of Sri Lanka as follows: -\n\n1. (1) This Act may be cited as the National Minimum Wage of Workers (Amendment) Act, No. of 2025.\n\n(2) The provisions of this Act shall be deemed to have come into operation on April 1, 2025."
