    "chunk_size_bytes": 1410,
    "chunk_text": "to amend the National Audit Act, No. 19 of 2018\n\nOrdered to be published by the Minister of Justice and Nationl Integration\n\nThis Gazette Supplement can be downloaded from www.documents.gov.lk\n\nNational Audit (Amendment)02\n\nSTATEMENT OF LEGAL EFFECT\n\n(a) to empower the Auditor-General to make recommendation to impose a surcharge\n\non the amount of any deficiency or loss in any transaction of an auditee entity to\n\nthe Surcharge Review Committee;\n\n(b) to empower the Surcharge Review Committee to consider the recommendations\n\nmade by the Auditor-General and to decide the amount to be imposed as a\n\nsurcharge; and\n\n(c) to specify the procedure to be adopted by the Surcharge Review Committee in\n\ndetermining the amount of surcharge and the recovery of the surcharge. Clause 7: This clause repeals section 20 of the principal enactment and is consequential to the amendment made to the principal enactment by clause 6 and clause 8. Clause 8: This clause amends section 21 of the principal enactment and the legal effect of the section as amended is to incorporate the provisions in the principle enactment to appoint the Surcharge Review Committee and to specify the composition thereof. Clause 9: This clause inserts new sections 21A, 21B, 21C, 21D, 21E and 21F in the principal enactment and the legal effect of the new sections is to provide for the provisions relating to the\n\n03National Audit (Amendment)"
