    "chunk_text": "Clause 7 : This clause amends section 341 of the principal enactment and is consequential to the amendment made by clause 4.\n\n01Penal Code (Amendment)\n\nShort title\n\nAmendment of section 308a of the principal enactment\n\nInsertion of new section 308b in the principal enactment\n\nAmendment of section 82 of Chapter 19\n\nL.D.-O 41/2024\n\nAn Act to amend the Penal Code (Chapter 19)\n\nBE it enacted by the Parliament of the Democratic Socialist Republic of Sri Lanka as follows: -\n\n1. This Act may be cited as the Penal Code (Amendment) Act, No. of 2025.\n\n2. Section 82 of the Penal Code (Chapter 19) (hereinafter referred to as the \u201cprincipal enactment\u201d) is hereby amended by the insertion immediately before the illustration to that section, of the following:-\n\n\u201cFifthly \u2013 That this exception shall not extend to the imposing of corporal punishment in respect of children.\u201d.\n\n3. Section 308a of the principal enactment is hereby amended in subsection (1) thereof, by the substitution for the word \u201cwilfully\u201d, of the word \u201cintentionally\u201d.\n\n4. The following new section is hereby inserted immediately after section 308a of the principal enactment and shall have effect as section 308b of that enactment: -\n\n308b. (1) Whoever, having the custody, charge, or care of any person under eighteen years of age, commits -\n\n(a) as a measure of punishment or correctional method, an act for which physical force is used, with knowledge that such act is likely to cause some degree of pain or discomfort however light; or\n\n5\n\n10\n\n15\n\n20\n\n25\n\nPenal Code (Amendment)02\n\n(b) non-physical act with knowledge that it is likely to cause humiliation however light,\n\ncommits the offence of corporal punishment."
