    "chunk_text": "Architects Law, No. 1 of 1976\n\nBE it enacted by the Parliament of the Democratic Socialist Republic of Sri Lanka as follows:-\n\n1. This Act may be cited as the Sri Lanka Institute of Architects (Amendment) Act, No. of 2025.\n\n\u201cWith effect from the date of coming into operation of this Act, the corporate members of the Institute shall consist of Fellows and Members:\u201d. 3. Section 12 of the principal enactment is hereby amended as follows:-\n\n(1) in subsection (1) thereof, by the substitution for the words \u201cand an Associate the initials \u201cA.I.A (Sri Lanka)\u201d.\u201d of the words \u201cand a Member the initials \u201cM.I.A (Sri Lanka)\u201d.\u201d ;\n\n(2) by the repeal of subsection (4) thereof, and the substitution therefor of the following :-\n\n5\n\n10\n\n15\n\n20\n\nSri Lanka Institute of Architects (Amendment)2\n\n\u201c(4) Except as provided in this section, no person or body of persons shall take or use the title \u201cChartered Architect\u201d or \u201cChartered Architects\u201d or the initials \u201cF.I.A (Sri Lanka)\u201d or \u201cM.I.A (Sri Lanka)\u201d, or use the same as the name or part of the name in any book, journal or other publication, dealing with architecture, design or the practice of architecture or the profession of architecture.\u201d.\n\n4. For the avoidance of doubts, it is hereby declared that, those who have been enrolled as Associates to the Institute on the day immediately preceding the date of coming into operation of this Act, shall, with effect from the date of coming into operation of this Act, be deemed to be members of the Institute.\n\n5. In the event of any inconsistency between the Sinhala and Tamil texts of this Act, the Sinhala text shall prevail.\n\nAvoidance of doubts\n\nSinhala text to prevail in case of inconsistency\n\n5\n\n10\n\n15\n\n3Sri Lanka Institute of Architects (Amendment)\n\nDEPARTMENT OF GOVERNMENT PRINTING"
