    "chunk_text": "Application for membership of the Institute\n\n8Institute of Real Estate Professionals Sri Lanka\n\n7. (1) Subject to the provisions of section 8, the period of membership of a member shall be a calendar year and be renewable.\n\n(3) The membership may be renewed on the payment of the renewal fee as may be specified by rules made under this Act.\n\n8. (1) A person shall be disqualified from being appointed or continuing as a member of the Council or the Institute, if such person -\n\n(a) has been or is under any law in force in Sri Lanka or in any other country found or declared to be of unsound mind;\n\n(b) has been or is adjudged an insolvent by a court of competent jurisdiction;\n\n(c) has served or is serving a sentence of imprisonment imposed by any court in Sri Lanka or any other country; or\n\n(d) has been found guilty of professional misconduct after an inquiry by the Council or a Committee appointed under section 18.\n\n(2) The Council shall have the power to disenroll any person who is a member of the Institute, if he becomes subject to any disqualification referred to in subsection (1):\n\nProvided however, the Council may, in lieu of disenrolling, suspend such person from membership for such period as the Council may deem fit:\n\n5\n\n10\n\n15\n\n20\n\n25\n\nPeriod of membership and renewal of membership\n\nDisqualificationsto be a member, disenrollment,disciplinary powers and procedure\n\n9Institute of Real Estate Professionals Sri Lanka\n\nProvided further, disenrollment shall not prevent the Council from subsequently re-enrolling such person, if satisfied that he is eligible to be enrolled.\n\n(3) No member of the Institute shall be disenrolled or suspended from membership, unless a Disciplinary Committee appointed by the Council under section 18, after inquiry, has submitted a report to the Council that such member has become disqualified to be a member of the Council under subsection (1) and has committed a professional misconduct."
